netflix had a tough first quarter it  reported the  first drop in subscribers in almost a  decade look at this chart we can see how  the number of subscribers grew and grew  and grew and then in this quarter it  dropped by 200 000  they expect it to drop by further 2  million in the upcoming quarter now why  is that it's partly to do with the end  of lockdowns people not having as much  time to spend in front of screens it's  partly to do with inflation with uh not  as much discretionary spending therefore  people cutting back on their netflix it  also has something to do with russia  where netflix has pulled out of but it  does have implications for the streaming  industry as a whole look at this chart  it's the price to earnings ratio for  netflix disney and paramount at the top  line the white one for netflix you can  see it used to traded a massive premium  to those other companies now disney  around the end of 2020  pivoted towards the netflix model it's  going to double down on disney plus  focus on being a growth stock that means  investors value it based on how big they  think it's going to be at some stage in  the future  but if you are a growth stop and growth  slows you get punished by investors and  so you can see here the white line of  netflix crossing below  disney as a valuation multiple  now what can netflix do to reignite  growth it basically has three tools it  can try to add more subscribers that's  clearly a struggle at the moment it can  increase prices also maybe a little bit  difficult given the inflationary context  the third thing and that's what it is  doing it is talking about advertising  and introducing an advertising funded  tier now the advantage of advertising is  it might only cost the user a few  dollars but the upside of what you can  make from advertisers themselves is  almost limitless you think about  facebook which makes something like 130  a year  from advertisers per user in the us  that's the growth strategy now for  netflix as it really struggles to add  new subs  you
 

